## 3. Codebase Analysis & Strategic Guidance

The following analysis is based on my direct review of the current codebase. Use these notes and tips to guide your implementation.

### Relevant Existing Code
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/api/rest/GiftCardResource.java`
    *   **Summary:** Exposes `/api/v1/gift-cards/*` and `/api/v1/admin/gift-cards/*` endpoints for balance checks, redemption, issuance, status updates, and ledger listings, translating domain models into DTOs through `GiftCardMapper` and enforcing idempotency via `X-Idempotency-Key`.
    *   **Recommendation:** Reuse this resource (and its pagination metadata helpers) for any new admin CRUD or checkout hooks instead of adding duplicate endpoints; always resolve tenant context via `TenantContext.getCurrentTenantId()` and return structured errors through the existing `ErrorResponse` wrapper.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/giftcard/GiftCardService.java`
    *   **Summary:** Implements secure code generation (SHA-256 hashed), issuance, redemption with pessimistic locking, refund/backfill operations, conversion to store credit, and Micrometer/reporting telemetry with dependencies on `CheckoutTenderService`, `ReportingProjectionService`, and `StoreCreditService`.
    *   **Recommendation:** Extend this service for any remaining acceptance-criteria gaps (audit messages, resend flows, refunds integration) rather than introducing parallel logic; every mutation should stay transactional, rely on `GiftCardTransaction` ledger writes, and forward events to `reportingProjectionService` plus tender tracking.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/storecredit/StoreCreditService.java`
    *   **Summary:** Owns store credit accounts per user, idempotent redemption, admin adjustments, and conversions initiated by gift cards while coordinating with checkout tender logging and projection reporting.
    *   **Recommendation:** Use `creditFromGiftCard()` and `redeem()` when integrating checkout/returns so that ledgers stay consistent; do not bypass helper methods that lock the account (`lockAccountByUser`) or skip Micrometer counters.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/test/java/villagecompute/storefront/giftcard/GiftCardServiceTest.java`
    *   **Summary:** Quarkus test suite that bootstraps tenants/users, issues cards, verifies redemption idempotency, ensures convert-to-store-credit flows, and cleans up Panache entities between runs.
    *   **Recommendation:** Mirror this pattern for any new integration tests (e.g., REST resources or refund contracts) so coverage stays ≥85%; use the provided helper methods for seeding gift cards and manipulating `TenantContext` in tests.

### Implementation Tips & Notes
*   **Tip:** DTOs for gift card operations already live in `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/api/types/`—extend them and `GiftCardMapper` when new fields (e.g., resend metadata, audit notes) surface to keep API responses aligned with OpenAPI.
*   **Tip:** `CheckoutTenderService` and `ReportingProjectionService` are mandatory touchpoints whenever balances shift; ensure new flows (refunds pushing value back to cards, conversions to credit) call both services so downstream reporting and SLA dashboards stay accurate.
*   **Tip:** Storefront/admin SPAs pull data via generated clients inside `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/api/generated/`; after updating `api/openapi.yaml`, rerun the generator so components like `GiftCardView.vue` or Pinia stores read the new schemas instead of hardcoding fetch calls.
*   **Tip:** Follow the existing security posture—never persist or log plaintext codes, always hash via `GiftCardService.hashCode()`, propagate `X-Idempotency-Key` headers, and guard admin endpoints with `@RolesAllowed({"admin"})`.
*   **Note:** No standalone `GiftCardView.vue` exists yet; base the new admin view under `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/modules/` (consistent with `loyalty` and `orders` modules), register its route via `router/index.ts`, and reuse shared components (e.g., `InlineAlert`, `MetricsCard`) plus i18n strings in `src/locales/*`.
*   **Warning:** All Panache entities for this module enforce tenant isolation; always fetch cards/accounts via the helper methods (`GiftCard.findByIdAndTenant`, locking queries) to avoid RLS violations, and ensure new SQL migrations keep `tenant_id` + auditing columns populated.
